Round 3 exploratory analyses in the paper: stored value vs reader, deletion taxonomy, query-time view, class composition

- Stage runs/stage6_ex_round3 (analysis/natural, store_reader, dm_deletion, view .json and a
  manifest with source-stage hashes and the producing commands), computed by the committed
  round-3 modules at f0f2e36 (clean tree) from the raw runs of stages e1, c and ctl;
  results_sources key ex_round3.
- analysis/ex_round3.py: ExRThree* macros (letters only) and five tables (tab_main_store,
  tab_store_reader, tab_store_reader_bxd, tab_dm_deletion, tab_view), wired into
  paper_numbers.build_macros and paper_tables.main; a CLI that reruns the four analyses and
  writes the stage manifest. numbers.tex only gains lines; every existing macro and table is
  byte-identical.
- Paper: Table 1 adds the store and reader parts of BxD (R2 W5); 4.1 states the all-item
  "by the shift" value as dilution by item class, with a marked \NatPending placeholder for
  block N (R2 W3); rule 3 and its evidence rewritten with the deletion taxonomy (R2 Q5);
  appendix paragraphs and tables for the store/reader split, the class composition, the
  deletion taxonomy and the query-time view on all items (R1 Q3); analysis-status row.
  Main text still ends on page 9.
- tests/test_ex_round3.py.

